{"component_id_namespace":"ec077a53-0b40-5f21-b1fe-a62094d2476b","component_schema":"exais.workbench_component.v1","components":[{"attributes":{"code":"TMC","legacy_node_id":"ks-topeka:tmc:13.10.680","page_type":"section"},"citation":"13.10.680","citation_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/13.10.680","content_hash":"3312859761b59e82c1faf38f2f3e9798bd4c18d549e15d36b8e35ff87b34607b","heading":"Water conservation stages – Stage 1, voluntary conservation measures.","ordinal":0,"parent_source_component_key":null,"schema":"exais.workbench_component.v1","source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:13.10.680:section","source_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/13.10.680","text":"When climatic conditions develop that indicate a water emergency may be declared, or whenever other emergencies that threaten the order, health, safety and general welfare of the public occur, the Director is authorized to request all consumers to:\n(a) Voluntarily implement even/odd day watering for exterior use.\n(b) Employ voluntary water conservation measures to limit or eliminate nonessential water uses including, but not limited to, the following:\n(1) Sprinkling of water on lawns, shrubs or trees.\n(2) Washing of automobiles, trucks and other vehicles.\n(3) Use of water in swimming pools, fountains and evaporative air conditioning systems.\n(4) Waste of water. (Code 1981 § 44-164(a). Code 1995 § 146-170.)","type":"section","workbench_component_id":"32f081b2-ed51-5fd2-94f1-e21060f6cbb3"},{"attributes":{"block_kind":"paragraph"},"citation":"13.10.680","citation_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/13.10.680","content_hash":"b85e0f84e0357c99b3cc59cdabca21effebcb95dcb1694e55894688b45fb1076","heading":null,"ordinal":0,"parent_source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:13.10.680:section","schema":"exais.workbench_component.v1","source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:13.10.680:block:0","source_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/13.10.680","text":"When climatic conditions develop that indicate a water emergency may be declared, or whenever other emergencies that threaten the order, health, safety and general welfare of the public occur, the Director is authorized to request all consumers to:","type":"paragraph","workbench_component_id":"77ede670-16e2-5f55-a5e1-f01c7d50e4b0"},{"attributes":{"block_kind":"paragraph"},"citation":"13.10.680","citation_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/13.10.680","content_hash":"5d7a9d8236e4f2aea2c67a5a887d621d7ba464ca64b81bdd4c03043dc51c1a62","heading":null,"ordinal":1,"parent_source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:13.10.680:section","schema":"exais.workbench_component.v1","source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:13.10.680:block:1","source_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/13.10.680","text":"(a) Voluntarily implement even/odd day watering for exterior use.","type":"paragraph","workbench_component_id":"854e9367-3466-5882-9c54-37d12d166a4c"},{"attributes":{"block_kind":"paragraph"},"citation":"13.10.680","citation_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/13.10.680","content_hash":"c92135b906348438aafac0f43e2eeae8d854102c4c7140a4573c66f13ffdb176","heading":null,"ordinal":2,"parent_source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:13.10.680:section","schema":"exais.workbench_component.v1","source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:13.10.680:block:2","source_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/13.10.680","text":"(b) Employ voluntary water conservation measures to limit or eliminate nonessential water uses including, but not limited to, the following:","type":"paragraph","workbench_component_id":"9ab946b2-0a14-5d91-84d2-2ff62a26fed9"},{"attributes":{"block_kind":"paragraph"},"citation":"13.10.680","citation_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/13.10.680","content_hash":"714a31cfe7bd9da9c0330b6ee1bbb0086dd39d0ae00f3caaba82c4a5d54ec5c8","heading":null,"ordinal":3,"parent_source_component_key":"ks